[ceiling] The front Z-slide heads' square catches stand at z=160.00 + 8.70 + 0.25 running clearance + 0.25 supported-face allowance = 169.20. Each overlaps the top's full-section foot and retains at least 3 mm of head stock. Lifting the seated top lands the flat foot on this face along the rail; its flat bearing resists lift without camming the seam open. The arm returns to the wall on its 45-degree under-flare, and slicer support carries the catch underside. The groove under the catch is open air from the arm's sliding face out past the exterior plane, so that support stands on the outside of the flank with a face exposed down the whole run; it comes off in one piece without reaching into the cavity. The tee carrier's flank window
interrupts each head over its own depth, so each catch runs as two faces either side of it.
